(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #103: overwriting a text field in a loop, each value
 built from the one before, leaves exactly the last value, and a copy of
 the thing taken part way through keeps the value of that moment. Sizes
 are printed, not the texts, so the output stays short.)

A thing called counter has
  a text called label is "",
  a number called count is 0.

a counter called tally.
a counter called snapshot.
For each n from 1 to 6000,
  Set tally's label to "{tally's label}x",
  Set tally's count to n,
  If n is 1000 then,
    Set snapshot to tally..
Print tally's count.
Print snapshot's count.
a buffer called whole.
append "{tally's label}" to whole.
a buffer called part.
append "{snapshot's label}" to part.
Print whole's size.
Print part's size.
